      {
        "tuple": "issue close",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Speech tier (operator-ruled 2026-09-02, CKCRED co-signed): closing a thread is reversible, creates no authority, lands no code. Evidence: fleet bots publicly listing fixed-but-open issues because close refused at admin; 30+ operator-bypass closes misattributed in ten days. --reason completed|not_planned is REQUIRED (distinct public statements); optional --comment rides as the body. Holder replies carry GitHub's returned state/state_reason verbatim; a failed comment after a successful state change is the partial outcome state_applied_comment_failed, never masked."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "issue reopen",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Speech tier, the inverse of issue close; declared together so a close is always reversible by the same seat."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "pr close",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Speech tier, same argument as issue close. In-row exclusion: --delete-branch / -d is refused by the shim before routing (gh_shim_destructive_flag) and no delete-branch field exists on the wire; branch deletion stays undeclared. pr merge stays admin."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "pr reopen",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Speech tier, the inverse of pr close; declared together because a PR's reopen is only CONDITIONALLY reversible (the head lives in the contributor's fork and can vanish) - specimen: a PR stuck closed-and-unmerged because reopen was unclassified under v11."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "issue create",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ]
      },
