        ],
        "reasoning": "Repo-lifecycle administration (visibility flips in public-flip ceremonies). Admin tier: refused for agents with GH_SHIM_BYPASS=operator named as remedy, so ceremonies are operator-executed by design. Declared as an argv tuple because v1 api_rules are GET-only (SEAM audit deferral): an api-form DELETE/PATCH row would be signed bytes the classifier cannot honor."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "run delete",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Actions-run deletion via gh's native verb (use `gh run delete`, not raw `api -X DELETE`, which stays unclassified). Admin tier for the same operator-executed-ceremony reason as `repo edit`; the refusal is loud on the FIRST attempt so a 309-run loop fails once, legibly, before the loop spends the ceremony window."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "run rerun",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "Administration: operator identity under the explicit audited bypass, never governed bot speech - a rerun has no public attribution surface, and granting speech Apps actions:write would widen the compromise surface. `run cancel` is deliberately undeclared beside this row: destructive and rare, the bypass must not enable it by accident."
      },
      {
        "tuple": "workflow run",
        "platform": [
          "macos",
          "linux"
        ],
        "reasoning": "CI dispatch for bound seats (E2E chaos-foundation gate). Admin tier, not governed: a workflow dispatch has no public attribution surface, so bot identity buys nothing - while granting speech Apps actions:write would let a stolen mint run arbitrary code. Operator identity via GH_SHIM_BYPASS=operator; authority is the agent's per the authority-vs-identity erratum."
